pygtk-posting (0.5.35) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add a Zebra label designer, powered by the LinuxZPL engine tracked as a
    git submodule, with label templates stored in the database.
  * Give the Zebra printers their own page in the Settings window.
  * Recover cleanly from a lost database connection: no more endless
    reconnect loops or a main loop spinning at 100% after a suspend.
  * Give worker-thread queries their own database connection.
  * Allow moving purchase order lines between orders and correcting a
    closed purchase order from the vendor payment window.
  * Open the contact and product editors directly from their hubs.
  * Ship the HTML invoice, finance charge and purchase order templates,
    which the package had been leaving out.
  * Build the package from the git file list; the version now lives in
    src/constants.py instead of the long-gone Anjuta Makefile.

 -- Reuben Rissler <pygtk.posting@gmail.com>  Fri, 11 Sep 2026 07:06:26 -0400
